{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/251440-wyrd-evolution-in-second-edition","id":251440,"title":"Wyrd Evolution in Second Edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-07T07:16:23-07:00","id":251440,"title":"Wyrd Evolution in Second Edition","content":"One of the things I'd like to see is the effects of a Wyrd increase being more prominent at a lower level. Changeling one of the venues where the splat has something that's somewhat human, becoming something else as the Wyrd is woven more into their form. As this is a foreign power that's coming in, it should have more immediate changes. As such, I think flavourfully, and mechanically, it'd offer some interesting consequences.<br /> <br /> Is growing your Wyrd a temptation? Unlike other games, the more Wyrd you have, the more similar to a Keeper you are. Why would one want to become more like /them/? Protection? Power to fight them off? Or is it possibly a way of coping? (Also, assuming the same benefits of Wyrd Evolution are the same, only starting at Wyrd 4 or so, it offers a benefit that I don't think is particularly unbalanced, as at the moment, they're at a stage which can hardly be utilized unless the game starts with a much higher XP level unless someone is home brewing).<br /> <br /> It offers an option of exploring what a Wyrd increase means. Is it allowing this outside power to come in and change one's self, or is it a Changeling taking advantage of this force, and through using it, becomes tainted, or just more attuned? In either case, I'm lead to believe this force is powerful, and this Too Solid Flesh, a curious introduction is in how mutable this flesh is. They're Changelings, after all, and putting some greater emphasis on the Change part of the name would help emphasize this. This would offer an opportunity of self exploration as a theme (I've seen Abuse Survivors tied to this re-write, I'm not married to that myself, but it'd allow such a situation as an inward look, and a reflection of what they've gone through, which is not something other splats offer as intrinsically).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/287-wildfire","name":"Wildfire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}